"CSS Object Model (CSSOM) Module Level 1 (https://drafts.csswg.org/cssom/)\nciteturn1224view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn1220view0\",\"lineno\":1457}); Total lines: 2901\nL1433:   1. If `property` is not a cite124†custom property , follow these substeps:\nL1434:     1. Let `property` be `property` cite147†converted to ASCII lowercase†infra.spec.whatwg.org .\nL1435:     2. If `property` is a shorthand property, follow these substeps:\nL1436:       1. Let `list` be a new array.\nL1437:       2. For each longhand property `longhand` that `property` maps to, append the result of invoking `cite704†getPropertyPriority() ` with `longhand` as argument to `list`.\nL1438:       3. If all items in `list` are the string \"`important`\", then return the string \"`important`\".\nL1439:   2. If `property` is a cite128†case-sensitive†w3c.github.io match for a cite654†property name of a cite653†CSS declaration in the cite602†declarations that has the cite665†important flag set, return the string \"`important`\".\nL1440:   3. Return the empty string.\nL1441: E.g. for `background-color:lime !IMPORTANT` the return value would be \"`important`\".\nL1442: \nL1443: The `setProperty(`property`, `value`, `priority`)` method must run these steps:\nL1444:   1. If the cite601†readonly flag is set, then cite200†throw†heycam.github.io a `cite781†NoModificationAllowedError†webidl.spec.whatwg.org ` exception.\nL1445:   2. If `property` is not a cite124†custom property , follow these substeps:\nL1446:     1. Let `property` be `property` cite147†converted to ASCII lowercase†infra.spec.whatwg.org .\nL1447:     2. If `property` is not a cite128†case-sensitive†w3c.github.io match for a cite125†supported CSS property , then return.\nL1448:   3. If `value` is the empty string, invoke `cite706†removeProperty() ` with `property` as argument and return.\nL1449:   4. If `priority` is not the empty string and is not an cite447†ASCII case-insensitive†infra.spec.whatwg.org match for the string \"`important`\", then return.\nL1450:   5. Let `component value list` be the result of cite789†parsing `value` for property `property`.\nL1451: Note: `value` can not include \"`!important`\".\nL1452:   6. If `component value list` is null, then return.\nL1453:   7. Let `updated` be false.\nL1454:   8. If `property` is a shorthand property, then for each longhand property `longhand` that `property` maps to, in canonical order, follow these substeps:\nL1455:     1. Let `longhand result` be the result of cite790†set the CSS declaration `longhand` with the appropriate value(s) from `component value list`, with the important flag set if `priority` is not the empty string, and unset otherwise, and with the list of declarations being the cite602†declarations .\nL1456:     2. If `longhand result` is true, let `updated` be true.\nL1457:   9. Otherwise, let `updated` be the result of cite790†set the CSS declaration `property` with value `component value list`, with the important flag set if `priority` is not the empty string, and unset otherwise, and with the list of declarations being the cite602†declarations .\nL1458:   10. If `updated` is true, cite782†update style attribute for the cite655†CSS declaration block .\nL1459: Tests\nL1460:   * cite791†cssom-setProperty-shorthand.html†wpt.fyi cite792†(live test)†wpt.live cite793†(source)†github.com L1461:   * cite794†MutationObserver-style.html†wpt.fyi cite795†(live test)†wpt.live cite796†(source)†github.com L1462:   * cite797†rule-restrictions.html†wpt.fyi cite798†(live test)†wpt.live cite799†(source)†github.com L1463:   * cite800†setproperty-null-undefined.html†wpt.fyi cite801†(live test)†wpt.live cite802†(source)†github.com L1464: To set a CSS declaration `property` with a value `component value list` and optionally with an important flag set, in a list of declarations `declarations`, the user agent must ensure the following constraints hold after its steps:\nL1465:   * Exactly one cite653†CSS declaration whose cite654†property name is a cite128†case-sensitive†w3c.github.io match of `property` must exist in `declarations`. Such declaration is referenced as the `target declaration` below.\nL1466:   * The `target declaration` must have value being `component value list`, and `target declaration`’s cite665†important flag must be cite661†set if important flag is set, and cite803†unset otherwise.\nL1467:   * Any cite653†CSS declaration which is not the `target declaration` must not be changed, inserted, or removed from `declarations`.\nL1468:   * If there are cite653†CSS declarations in `declarations` whose cite654†property name is in the same cite671†logical property group as `property`, but has a different cite672†mapping logic , `target declaration` must be at an index after all of those CSS declarations.\nL1469:   * The steps must return true if the serialization of `declarations` was changed as result of the steps. It may return false otherwise.\nL1470: Should we add something like \"Any observable side effect must not be made outside `declarations`\"? The current constraints sound like a hole for undefined behavior.\nL1471: \nL1472: Note: The steps of cite790†set a CSS declaration are not defined in this level of CSSOM. User agents may use different algorithms as long as the constraints above hold.\nL1473: The simplest way to conform with the constraints would be to always remove any existing declaration matching `property`, and append the new declaration to the end. But based on implementation feedback, this approach would likely regress performance.\nL1474: \nL1475: Another possible algorithm is:\nL1476:   1. If `property` is a cite128†case-sensitive†w3c.github.io match for a cite654†property name of a cite653†CSS declaration in `declarations`, follow these substeps:\nL1477:     1. Let `target declaration` be such cite653†CSS declaration .\nL1478:     2. Let `needs append` be false.\nL1479:     3. cite804†For each†infra.spec.whatwg.org `declaration` in `declarations` after `target declaration`:\nL1480:       1. If `declaration`’s cite654†property name is not in the same cite671†logical property group as `property`, then cite662†continue†infra.spec.whatwg.org .\nL1481:       2. If `declaration`’ cite654†property name has the same cite672†mapping logic as `property`, then cite662†continue†infra.spec.whatwg.org .\nL1482:       3. Let `needs append` be true.\nL1483:       4. cite805†Break .\nL1484:     4. If `needs append` is false, then:\nL1485:       1. Let `needs update` be false.\nL1486:       2. If `target declaration`’s cite806†value is not equal to `component value list`, then let `needs update` be true.\nL1487:       3. If `target declaration`’s cite665†important flag is not equal to whether important flag is set, then let `needs update` be true.\nL1488:       4. If `needs update` is false, then return false.\nL1489:       5. Set `target declaration`’s cite806†value to `component value list`.\nL1490:       6. If important flag is set, then set `target declaration`’s cite665†important flag , otherwise unset it.\nL1491:       7. Return true.\nL1492:     5. Otherwise, remove `target declaration` from `declarations`.\nL1493:   2. Append a new cite653†CSS declaration with cite654†property name `property`, cite806†value `component value list`, and cite665†important flag set if important flag is set to `declarations`.\nL1494:   3. Return true.\nL1495: The `removeProperty(`property`)` method must run these steps:\nL1496:   1. If the cite601†readonly flag is set, then cite200†throw†heycam.github.io a `cite781†NoModificationAllowedError†webidl.spec.whatwg.org ` exception.\nL1497:   2. If `property` is not a cite124†custom property , let `property` be `property` cite147†converted to ASCII lowercase†infra.spec.whatwg.org .\nL1498:   3. Let `value` be the return value of invoking `cite703†getPropertyValue() ` with `property` as argument.\nL1499:   4. Let `removed` be false.\nL1500:   5. If `property` is a shorthand property, for each longhand property `longhand` that `property` maps to:\nL1501:     1. If `longhand` is not a cite654†property name of a cite653†CSS declaration in the cite602†declarations , cite662†continue†infra.spec.whatwg.org .\nL1502:     2. Remove that cite653†CSS declaration and let `removed` be true.\nL1503:   6. Otherwise, if `property` is a cite128†case-sensitive†w3c.github.io match for a cite654†property name of a cite653†CSS declaration in the cite602†declarations , remove that CSS declaration and let `removed` be true.\nL1504:   7. If `removed` is true, cite782†Update style attribute for the cite655†CSS declaration block .\nL1505:   8. Return `value`.\nL1506: The `parentRule` attribute must return the cite604†parent CSS rule .\nL1507: \nL1508: The `cssFloat` attribute, on getting, must return the result of invoking `cite703†getPropertyValue() ` with `float` as argument. On setting, the attribute must invoke `cite705†setProperty() ` with `float` as first argument, as second argument the given value, and no third argument. Any exceptions thrown must be re-thrown.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCSS Object Model (CSSOM) Module Level 1 (https://drafts.csswg.org/cssom/)\nciteturn1224view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn1220view0\",\"lineno\":1495}); Total lines: 2901\nL1467:   * Any cite653†CSS declaration which is not the `target declaration` must not be changed, inserted, or removed from `declarations`.\nL1468:   * If there are cite653†CSS declarations in `declarations` whose cite654†property name is in the same cite671†logical property group as `property`, but has a 